$ docker compose up

{ Simple example

  { docker-compose.yaml

code {
services:
  database:
    image: pgvector/pgvector:0.7.2-pg16
    restart: always
    environment:
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: admin
      POSTGRES_USER: admin
      POSTGRES_DB: renes-test-db
    ports:
      - 5432:5432
code }

  }
  { Running the container

code {
$ → development/tools/Docker/commands/compose up -d
code }

code {
→ development/databases/PostgreSQL/psql -h localhost -p 5432 -U admin -d renes-test-db
code }

    Alternatively, direct connection inside the container:
code {
docker compose exec database psql -U admin -d renes-test-db
code }

  }
  { Remove container and image

code {
docker compose down
docker image rm pgvector/pgvector:0.7.2-pg16
code }

    Alternatively, in one go:
code {
docker compose down --rmi all
code }

    Verification:
code {
docker container ls -a
docker image ls
code }

  }

}
